stages.goal:
Prove on the exact scorer stack (10-12 wheelhouse: vllm 0.19.1 re-patched, adk_submission 0.2.13; TP4 on 4xL4) that an r16 adapter on all 7 projections, with the duplicated v_proj:
(i) starts at gmu 0.80 and 0.90 with adk's own flags;
(ii) leaves room for at least one 32,768-token request;
(iii) changes the logits;
(iv) survives a 16k-token prompt_logprobs request, which E0 parity needs.
What it teaches:
- How vLLM multi-LoRA uses memory: one slot, a rank bucket, LoRA buffers taken from the KV budget, and prompt-logprob logits that the memory profiler does not count.
- How to test 'is the adapter applied' with temperature-0 logprobs.

Measure the deployment config v3t_think on the new harness:
- per-task time for the 12 h projection;
- per-call behaviour: thought tokens, length finishes, overflows, compactions;
- the dev score;
- capture correctness on a live vLLM.
If it is clean, it becomes our next submission.

Thinking stays ON. A thinking-off arm is not run by default: one run per arm cannot overturn the external evidence (Ayush 23 vs 48-51/129, all public 0.17-0.18 configs), and dropping it saves about 1.1 h.

What it teaches:
- Calibrating a time budget from measurements.
- Why the training data must be generated in the exact deployment format (the budgets are printed in the task prompt).

stages.files_to_create_or_change:
No new files beyond Stage 0.

Build (GMU default 0.90, no adapter):
  python scripts/kaggle_build.py agent_eval --split dev --submission think=experiments/v3t_think --env CAPTURE=1 --push
Collect:
  kaggle kernels output <owner>/gemma-agent-eval -p eval/runs/t0

Local analysis
- python scripts/compare_runs.py think=<run dir> --max-minutes 5.0
- From the captures, using scratch dp/convert_captures.py helpers:
  - thought tokens per call (between <|channel> and <channel|> in completion_token_ids);
  - share of calls that hit the 4,096 thought budget;
  - share of 'length' finishes;
  - per-call overflow errors (proxy status 400, or vLLM 'maximum context length');
  - compactions per task;
  - share of calls with visible text next to a tool call;
  - share of empty thought blocks.
- Capture checks:
  - '<|think|>' appears in the system turn;
  - the system text ends with the ADK identity line;
  - earlier calls in the turn are preceded by a thought block (template lines 237-240);
  - after a compaction the prompt contains 'For context:[model] said:';
  - the stop token 50 or 106 is present in completion_token_ids;
  - >= 95% of agent calls are captured with non-null ids.
- Run the converter with an --allow-dev smoke flag and delete its output. Dev data is never trained on.
- Write eval/decision_sets.json dev_dec.

Prompt-only submission (if the gate passes):
  python scripts/build_submission.py --submission-dir experiments/v3t_think --overhead-minutes 0.5
The user submits dist/v3t_think/submission.zip. Nothing is pending now; the queue is about 33 h.

Conditional T0b (only if a pathology flag fires):
  python scripts/kaggle_build.py agent_eval --splits-file eval/decision_sets.json --split dev_fair --submission think2=experiments/v3t_think --submission off=experiments/v3t_off --push

stages.success_criteria:
- The run finishes and the captures pass the checks above.
- Projection: 120 × (variant hours / 33) + 0.2 <= 10.5 h. This uses measured hours including setup and verification, and the dev mix includes 15 tasks that hit the cap.
- Pathology flags all clear:
  - core >= 5/6;
  - resolved >= 7/33 (historical thinking-off mean 9.7, SD 1.5);
  - 'length' finishes <= 2% of calls;
  - 0 per-call overflows.
- Submission gate: run finished, 0 overflow, core >= 5/6, projection <= 10.5 h. There is no score threshold, because neither dev noise nor the leaderboard (±2.5 tasks) could resolve one.
- Recorded for later stages: s/task by tier, s/LLM call (forum 746250 expects about 8.7 s), thought tokens per call, and the content-reordered and empty-thought rates (these size Stage 4).

stages.gpu_hours:
About 3.25 h of 4xL4 wall time (6.5 quota-h), range 3.0-3.5:
- smoke test about 2 min;
- load and quantize 5-15 min (unknown);
- training guard 2.75 h (about 1.19M tokens at an estimated 120 tok/s);
- 2 val passes and the save.
Lightning: 0 Kaggle hours.

stages.success_criteria:
Early stop after E1 (NO-GO, skip E2) if any of:
- the summed delta over pairs 1-2 is <= -2;
- any LoRA arm has core < 5/6;
- any overflow, crash or undeclared-tool error;
- LoRA s/task > 1.15 × control s/task.

GO after E2 needs all of:
- mean delta >= +1.5 tasks per run (b - c >= 6 over 4 pairs);
- exact one-sided McNemar p <= 0.05 on the discordant task-run cells;
- LoRA keeps core in >= 23 of 24 core cells;
- malformed calls <= 2 per run;
- repeat% <= 6;
- overflow 0;
- projected scorer runtime <= 10.5 h: Stage 2's full-dev hours scaled by the LoRA/control s/task ratio on dev_dec.

Why this bar:
- Per-run SD on the decision set is about 1.1-1.5 tasks (historical per-task rates give 1.14), so a paired difference has SD about 1.6-2.1. With 4 pairs the SE is about 0.8-1.05, so +1.5 is about 1.4-1.9 SE.
- McNemar caps the false-GO rate at 5%.
